CORE libstdcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ output before main reaches the buffer: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ cin tied to cout: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ clog not tied: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ wcin tied to wcout: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.5\] line \d+ wcerr tied to wcout: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.6\] line \d+ wcerr unitbuf: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.7\] line \d+ cerr good or bad after output: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.8\] line \d+ cin.get in range: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.9\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The standard stream objects, defined in the compiled library, were
nondeterministic.  They are now defined and constructed before the
program's own objects of static storage duration.
